      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The original has these understandability issues:\n1. `years0.ONE` accesses a static field through an instance variable — confusing and bad practice\n2. `years0` is only created to serve as a vehicle for accessing `Years.ONE`\n3. Variable names `years0` / `years1` are not descriptive\n4. Test method name `test11` tells nothing about intent\n\nLet me write the improved version:The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test removes the unnecessary `Years.ZERO` intermediate variable (which was only used to access the static `ONE` field through an instance), uses `Years.ONE` directly, and renames the variable and method to clearly express the intent: dividing `Years.ONE` by 1 returns the same one-year value, which is not zero."
